0,Roglai language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roglai_language,"The Roglai language is a Chamic language of southern Vietnam, spoken by the Raglai people. There are four Roglai dialects: Northern, Du Long, Southern, and Cac Gia.","Roglai, Northern",Austronesian
1,Chamic languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chamic_languages,"The Chamic languages are a subgroup of Malayo-Polynesian languages in the Austronesian family. The ancestor of this subfamily, proto-Chamic, is associated with the Sa Huỳnh culture, its speakers arriving in what is now Vietnam from Formosa.","Roglai, Northern",Austronesian
2,"Roglai, Northern language - Global Recordings Network",https://globalrecordings.net/en/language/rog,"Audio recordings available in Roglai, Northern These recordings are designed for evangelism and basic Bible teaching to bring the gospel message to people who are not literate or are from oral cultures, particularly unreached people groups.","Roglai, Northern",Austronesian
